1997 Apr 14: [rwp]

   Modified InitDiskTable.c to make it a little more sophisticated vis-a-vis
   errors on trying to validate spool devices.

   Modified Caliban.c as follows: 

1) Call to InitDiskTables now just looks at the number of valid devices
   detected, now kept out of the disktab structure, but in the new numvalid
   variable.  
   If numvalid=0, prints an error 
   If numvalid<disktab->numdisks, prints a warning to the effect that the
   Caliban.ini file contains invalid spool devices

2) CHKSTATUS command, now prints the status of all spool devices in the
   Caliban.ini file.  As before, it would only print the first (0:numvalid) as
   it did not check the "valid" flag on the loop.  This was confusing, as we
   had the situation that 4 spool devs were in the .ini file, but only 2 were
   valid.  If the first 2 spool devices in Caliban.ini were valid, they would
   get printed, but if the first two were invalid, they were not printed, as
   the printout only looped 0:1 instead of 0:3.  We need to know if a disk
   came up invalid on startup, so we now print the whole table

