1997 September 4: [brh]

   Fixed problem resulting from embedded nulls in FITS filename and uniquename
   header cards.  Previously, Caliban assumed the last character of every card
   value was a quote.  If the filename was less than 8 characters and the
   filename ended with a null, Caliban was blindly chopping the last
   character, thinking it was a null.  Now it first checks to make sure the
   last character is a quote before chopping.

   Fixed problem with null padding on FITS data segment.  Pad buffer contained
   garbage character in first byte since pad constructor loop control variable
   initialized to 1 instead of 0.

1997 October 2: [brh]

   Fixed problem with FITS segment padding routine where if header or data
   segment worked out to an exact multiple of 2880, a pad of 2880 was added.

   Added STATUS: MACHINETYPE=DOWNSTREAM reply to PONG.

   Fixed problem where spurious carriage return (\r) characters appearing on
   the end of messages sent to XmitMsg routine would cause the message to be
   displayed and then immediately overwritten on the screen or when viewing
   the log file, thus making it appear as though the messages were never
   there.

   Added FITS_DATA_BLOCK_SIZE constant to allow changing block size for FITS
   data segment transfers.

   Changed the way FITS header segment is read so that once the header size is
   discovered, a buffer is allocated such that the header segment can be
   read/written in one chunk.

