2005 Feb 17: [rwp]

    GCC no longer implements varargs.h, instead use stdarg.h.  This
    means changes to XmitMsg.c and its prototype.

      substitute stdarg.h for varargs.h

      change proto to "XmitMsg(int port, ...)" in Caliban.h and XmitMsg.c

      In XmitMsg.c

        comment out:

	    int port;
	    port = va_arg();

        remove

	    old function declaration and "va_dcl"

	modify

	    va_start(paramlist) --> va_start(paramlist,port);

        
    and recompile.  stdarg is apparently ANSI and POSIX, varargs is
    not.  Since GCC no longer supports it, neither do we.


2007 August: [rwp]

    Major modifications in various areas:

    1) Added option to require ACK SWAP in response to REQ SWAP, with up
       to 3 attempts before fail-over.  Requires major changes to the
       select() loop in main to permit checking.  Can be enabled on
       startup with the ACKSWAP keyword.  During runtime it can be
       changed within the session with +/-ACKSWAP.  The timeout interval
       is set at startup by the TIMEOUT keyword, in integer seconds,
       or during a session with TIMEOUT nnn.

    2) Added new command RECOVER n disk, to force-read n images from
       the named disk. Thus, "RECOVER 50 DISK1" will attempt to read
       up to 50 FITS images from DISK1 onto the Linux disk.  Used to
       recover data from the transfer disks when there is a synch failure.
       Note that you must synch with the IC to get the blocksize right.

    3) Minor changes in the code to make error and warning state trapping
       better and more transparent to the user.  Fixed an unexpected oversight
       in not informing the exposure request host that we had to revert
       to a UNIQNAME filename to avoid overwrite.  

    4) Added color to warnings, errors, and fatal errors to hopefully
       catch the observer's attention on a busy workstation screen.

    5) Fixed long-standing bug if END gets too close to a disk sector
       boundary.  This seemed to affect OSIRIS more than others.



